{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>כי שם ה' אקרא.</b> Here כי serves in the sense of 'when,' as in ״כִּי תָבֹאוּ אֶל הָאָרֶץ״ (Leviticus 23) — when I call upon and proclaim the name of YHWH, you <b>ascribe greatness to our Elohim</b> and bless His name. From here the Sages said that one answers 'Blessed be the name of His glorious kingdom' after a blessing in the Sanctuary (see Sifrei; Mekhilta Exodus 13; Berakhot 21; Ta'anit 16)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:07.456639623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}